message.content:
{
  "summary": "This bill would require local education agencies (LEAs) to classify school nurses as licensed personnel and pay them according to the LEA's salary schedule for licensed personnel. School nurses employed by an LEA who are registered nurses and Nationally Certified School Nurses with zero years of experience must receive the same base salary as licensed teachers with a bachelor's degree and zero years of experience. Nurses with more training and experience than these requirements must receive more than that base salary, while those with less must receive less. The bill prohibits an LEA from reducing a school nurse's salary when adopting a salary schedule. These rules do not apply to LEA contractors or the LEA's ability to contract with the Tennessee public school nurse program. The bill would take effect July 1, 2026, and apply to the 2026-2027 school year and beyond."
}
